        "content": "Focus on three core sub-dimensions: (1) Writing & Terminology: Check for grammatical errors, typos, and inconsistent terminology (e.g., capitalization, abbreviations). Ensure experimental setups and hyperparameters are detailed enough for reproducibility, including specific architecture modifications. (2) Notation: Verify mathematical symbols are consistent and defined before use. Flag variable name collisions (e.g., using 'x' for both input and a parameter range). (3) Figures: Ensure captions are complete, defining axes, legends, and subplot conditions. Check for ambiguous labels in multi-panel figures. Common pitfalls include disjointed results sections (scattering results by attack vs. network type) and vague descriptions of 'parameter equivalence'. Best practices: Suggest restructuring results for logical flow (grouping by attack or network type), providing summary tables, and performing thorough language edits.",
